      },
      "body": "## Problem\n\n`_extract_endpoint_context()` caches endpoint metadata by `id(func)` without retaining or validating the function object. After an endpoint is collected, Python can reuse that id for another endpoint, causing validation errors and logs to report the wrong file, line, or function.\n\n## Solution\n\nStore a weak reference alongside each cached context and validate the referenced object with `is` before using a cache hit. Callable objects that do not support weak references are still handled correctly and are recomputed instead of being retained.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_endpoint_context_cache.py tests/test_custom_route_class.py tests/test_custom_middleware_exception.py tests/test_callable_endpoint.py` (9 passed)\n- `uv run mypy fastapi/routing.py` (passed)\n- `uv run ty check fastapi/routing.py` (passed)\n- `uv run bash scripts/test.sh` (3,347 passed, 18 skipped, 5 xfailed locally; the optional CLI test was unavailable because `fastapi[standard]` was not installed)\n- Fork preflight run [35815265234](https://github.com/rksharma-owg/fastapi/actions/runs/35815265234) passed the full test script on Ubuntu 3.13, macOS 3.10, and Windows 3.12 for commit `22229c3e9fa86e8f95fb8d926bcdde63bab5f5fa`.\n\nFixes #16390\n",
      "changed_files": 2,
